CHANNEL SIGNATURE GENERATION

1. Request
    Channel will send below Request to business service
    {
      "requestId":"EQUITY10001112003136",
      "channelId":"STK",
      "sourceSystemId":"EQUITEL_STK",
      "callbackURL":"http://localhost:8085/v1/callback/channel",
      "sourceTranType":"1",
      "sourceAccount":"1001008010940",
      "sourceCountryCode":"54",
      "sourceCurrency":"KES",
      "senderName":"KATEIS & OLE NASHUU",
      "senderInstitutionCode":"0068",
      "senderPhone":"+254-720000000",
      "receiverAccount":"0170197176640", 
      "receiverInstitutionCode":"0012", 
      "receiverCurrency":"KES",
      "amount": "500",
      "feeAmount":"0.00",
      "paymentReason":"Payments",
      "narration":"Pesalink's Transfer",
      "signature":"Generate Signature"
    }

2. Channel ID and Source System ID
    The following will be used for Channel Id and Source System ID

        CHANNEL_ID     :   SOURCE_SYSTEM
        1. STK         :   EQUITEL_STK        
        2. APP         :   EQUITY_APP
        3. WEB         :   EQUITY_WEB
        4. USSD        :   EQUITY_USSD
        5. EAZAPP      :   EAZZY_APP
        6. EAZNET      :   EAZZY_NET
        7. EAZBIZ      :   EAZZY_BIZ
        8. EVA         :   CHATBOT_EVA        
        9. OTC         :   BRANCH

3. Generate Key Pairs and certificates
    For each channel Id, the sending channel will generate a key pair and a certificate
    Use KeyStore Type = PKCS12

    Example: STK channel
    i. KeyPair Generation
        keytool -genkeypair -alias EquitelSTK_KeyPair -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -dname "CN=EquitelSTK" -validity 365 -storetype PKCS12 -keystore EquitelSTK.p12 -storepass 190875kLDDfwZE
    
    ii. Certificate generation
        keytool -exportcert -alias EquitelSTK_KeyPair -storetype PKCS12 -keystore EquitelSTK.p12 -file EQUITEL_STK.cer -rfc -storepass 190875kLDDfwZE
    
4. Share the certiface with us once it's generated.

5. Field Used To Generate Clear Text For Hashing
    Channel will use the below request fields for hashing during signature generation;
        clearText = requestId
            + channelId
            + sourceSystemId
            + sourceAccount
            + sourceCurrency
            + senderName
            + senderInstitutionCode
            + receiverAccount
            + receiverInstitutionCode
            + receiverCurrency
            + amount
            + feeAmount

6. Digital Signature Generation
   i. Using the clearText, Private Key and algorithm, sign the request:

    Where: 
        a. clearText = clearText in step 5
        b. privateKey = generated primary key in step 3
        c. algorithm = SHA256withRSA

            public class SignMsg {
            private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SignMsg.class);

            @Value("${encrypt.key-store.algorithm}")
            private String algorithm;

            @Autowired
            TelemetryClient telemetryClient;

            public byte[] signMessage(String theXsumFields, PrivateKey privatekey, ErrorStatus errorStatus) {
                byte[] messageBytes = theXsumFields.getBytes();
                byte[] digitalSignature;
                Signature signature;
                try {
                    signature = Signature.getInstance(algorithm);
                    signature.initSign(privatekey);
                    signature.update(messageBytes);
                    digitalSignature = signature.sign();
                } catch (SignatureException | NoSuchAlgorithmException | InvalidKeyException ex) {
                    errorStatus.setStatus("Failed");
                    errorStatus.setStatusCode("01");
                    errorStatus.setStatusDesc("SignatureException Occurred");
                    log.error("SignatureException: " + ex.getMessage());
                    telemetryClient.trackTrace("SignatureException: " + ex.getMessage(), SeverityLevel.Error);
                    return null;
                }
                return digitalSignature;
            }
        }

    ii. Encode the signature with Base64
